      "notes": "**Sandisk (SNDK): news from 2026-09-28 to 2026-10-28**\n\nSandisk reports fiscal Q1 2027 results on 2026-10-29 after the close, so they are not yet out.\n\n**1. Guidance and results**\n- No guidance change, withdrawal or pre-announcement found inside the window.\n- Operative Q1 FY27 guidance, given with Q4 results: revenue $10.3–10.8B and non-GAAP EPS of about $45. This is a secondary source. — 2026-08-05 (date inferred from the earnings calendar) — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/prediction-sandisk-stock-soar-oct-153601931.html\n- Q4 FY26 non-GAAP EPS was $39.25 against a $34.59 forecast, and revenue was $8.97B against $8.42B. The shares fell 12.1% after hours. — 2026-08-05 — https://www.investing.com/equities/sandisk-corp-earnings\n- Consensus for the Oct 29 report differs by source. Barchart has EPS of $45.22 — 2026-10-26 — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/sandisk-earnings-preview-expect-123010342.html. TipRanks has $46.67 — date unknown — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/sndk/earnings\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- Cantor Fitzgerald maintained Overweight and cut its price target to $2,200 from $2,900. — 2026-10-26 — https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SNDK/\n- Mizuho (Vijay Rakesh) raised its target to $2,050 from $1,875 and kept a Buy. TheStreet dates this Oct 5 — 2026-10-05 — https://www.thestreet.com/investing/stocks/sndk-sandisk-stock-price-target-mizuho-october-2026. StockAnalysis dates it Oct 6 — 2026-10-06 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/sndk/forecast/\n- Citi maintained Buy with a $2,100 target. — 2026-10-09 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/sndk/forecast/\n- Bernstein maintained Buy with a $3,000 target. — 2026-10-05 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/sndk/forecast/\n- Zacks Research upgraded the stock from Hold to Strong-Buy. — 2026-10-13 — https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NASDAQ/SNDK/forecast/\n- Weiss Ratings downgraded it from Buy (B-) to Hold (C+). — 2026-10-14 — https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NASDAQ/SNDK/forecast/\n- Rosenblatt initiated at Buy with a $2,400 target. This falls just before the window. — 2026-09-21 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/sndk/forecast/\n- Consensus targets differ by source. MarketBeat has $2,120.65 — 2026-10-22 — https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NASDAQ/SNDK/forecast/. StockAnalysis has $2,143.83 — date unknown — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/sndk/\n\n**3. Litigation and regulation**\n- Nothing material found in the window. I found no new lawsuits, investigations, fines, export-control actions or approvals.\n- The FY26 10-K gives only generic risk language on litigation and investigations. — date unknown — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000162828026057406/sndk-20260703.htm\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- Sandisk was named exclusive storage partner for Meta VR Glasses, with microSD Express cards and USB-C drives planned around a spring 2027 launch. This is a secondary source. — 2026-10-14 — https://tech-insider.org/nand-shortage-ssd-prices-2026/\n- Background from before the window: a post on X summarizing the Q4 call says Sandisk has agreements with 8 data-center and edge customers. They carry $93.9B of minimum expected revenue and $16.5B of financial guarantees. This is a low-quality source. — 2026-08-05 — https://x.com/TheValueist/status/2085131426467319824\n- No customer losses or contract changes found in the window.\n\n**5. Insider activity**\n\nAll items below are sales under Rule 10b5-1 plans. I found no purchases.\n- In the window: Chief Legal Officer Bernard Shek sold 600 shares at $1,734.94, leaving 25,588. — 2026-10-01 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000124264826000045/edgardoc.xml\n- Shek's pattern is 600 shares on the first trading day of each month, including 2026-09-01 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000136324926000074/edgardoc.xml\n- Shek also sold 2,308 shares at $1,767.33 under the same plan. — 2026-09-08 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000124264826000027/edgardoc.xml\n- Selling clustered just before the window:\n  - CFO Luis Visoso sold 1,000 shares at $1,568.83. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000124264826000033/edgardoc.xml\n  - CEO David Goeckeler sold at about $1,522–1,538 per share. — 2026-09-14 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000124264826000032/edgardoc.xml\n  - Goeckeler sold again at about $1,567–1,577 per share. — 2026-09-17 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000124264826000041/edgardoc.xml\n  - CTO Alper Ilkbahar also sold. — 2026-09-03 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000124264826000028/edgardoc.xml\n- Plan capacity per the 10-K: Goeckeler up to 124,192 shares, Visoso up to 11,000, and Ilkbahar up to 6,270. — date unknown — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002023554/000130817926000425/sndk015568-ars.pdf\n- My searches returned no other Form 4s dated Oct 2–28. That doesn't prove none were filed.\n\n**6. Product and competitive news**\n- Sandisk launched the Guardian Series high-endurance memory cards, starting at $28.99 for 32GB. — 2026-10-13 — https://tech-insider.org/nand-shortage-ssd-prices-2026/\n- The same source reports SK hynix and Sandisk announced the first High Bandwidth Flash standard specs at FMS 2026. — 2026-10-21 — https://tech-insider.org/nand-shortage-ssd-prices-2026/\n- The NAS 600 and NAS 800 SSDs were unveiled earlier, went on sale in September and are spreading to more international retail channels in October. — 2026-08-20 — https://tech-insider.org/sandisk-nas-600-nas-800-ssd-launch-2026/\n- Competitor moves in October:\n  - Samsung unveiled the PM1763 Gen6 and BM1773 256TB enterprise SSDs at the OCP summit, and Kioxia introduced the E1.L QLC SSDs (sampling). — 2026-10-09 (Kioxia date; Samsung date unknown) — https://tech-insider.org/nand-shortage-ss",
